Thought: To generate a diverse list of nitride compositions and retrieve their polymorphs, I need to first identify a list of nitride compositions. Then, I will use the `batch_retrieve_polymorphs` tool to get polymorphs for these compositions. I will ensure that the parameters `max_energy_above_hull`, `max_per_composition`, and `max_compositions` are set according to the task requirements.
Action: batch_retrieve_polymorphs
Action Input: {"compositions": ["AlN", "GaN", "InN", "BN", "Si3N4", "TiN", "ZrN", "HfN", "VN", "NbN", "TaN", "CrN", "MoN", "WN", "ScN", "YN", "LaN", "CeN", "PrN", "NdN", "SmN", "EuN", "GdN", "TbN", "DyN", "HoN", "ErN", "TmN", "YbN", "LuN", "ThN", "UN", "PuN", "NpN", "AmN", "CmN", "BkN", "CfN", "EsN", "FmN"], "max_energy_above_hull": 0.3, "max_per_composition": 3, "save_directory": "/Users/n0w0f/chained_ml_gpt_react_nitride/batch_retrieve_nitride_polymorphs_trial_1"}

